Manager, you can test the deployed gateway in three ways:

---

### 1. Browser Quick Test (Fastest)
Open these URLs in your browser after deployment:

| Test | URL |
|------|-----|
| **Health Check** | `https://rose-beeper-gateway.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev/health` |
| **Get 10 Quotes** | `https://rose-beeper-gateway.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev/?count=10` |
| **Get 3 Quotes** | `https://rose-beeper-gateway.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev/?count=3` |

If you see JSON arrays like this, it's working:
```json
[
  {"idx":6,"content":"Nỗi sợ...","context":"...","date":"2021~2023","specific":"Đàn ông thích mèo...","container":"Spiderum - Linh Vũ","cat":"writing","tags":["#Heartbroken"]},
  {"idx":1,"content":"Static, hum, tum, needle drops...","context":"","date":"2025-07","specific":"Vinyl Angel","container":"Koi no Koe","cat":"music","tags":["#Acoustic"]}
]
```

---

### 2. Terminal Test (From Your Terminal)
If you give me the worker URL, I can run automated tests from here:

```bash
# Replace with your actual worker URL
WORKER_URL="https://rose-beeper-gateway.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev"

# Health check
curl "https://rose-beeper-gateway.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev/health"

# Get 10 quotes
curl "https://rose-beeper-gateway.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev/?count=10"
```

---

### 3. ESP32 Test (Real Hardware)
Flash this minimal sketch to your ESP32:

```cpp
#include <WiFi.h>
#include <HTTPClient.h>
#include <ArduinoJson.h>

void fetchQuotes() {
  HTTPClient http;
  http.begin("https://rose-beeper-gateway.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev/?count=10");
  int code = http.GET();
  if (code == 200) {
    DynamicJsonDocument doc(4096);
    deserializeJson(doc, http.getString());
    JsonArray quotes = doc.as<JsonArray>();

    Serial.printf("Received %d quotes!\n", quotes.size());
    for (JsonObject q : quotes) {
      long idx = q["idx"];
      const char* text = q["content"];
      const char* auth = q["container"];
      Serial.printf("#%ld by %s\n", idx, auth);
    }
  }
  http.end();
}

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(115200);
  WiFi.begin("YOUR_SSID", "YOUR_PASSWORD");
  while (WiFi.status() != WL_CONNECTED) delay(500);
  fetchQuotes();
}

void loop() {}
```

---

